{"id": "EUVD-2026-75100", "enisaUuid": "1e405ecc-cd25-3c99-848b-50270877b5b4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxhci: dbgtty: Fix unregister on tty_register_driver() failure\n\nIf tty_register_driver() fails, it drops the reference, but fails to set\nthe global dbc_tty_driver to NULL, causing the unregister to be called\nagain when module exits.\n\nOn module unload dbc_tty_exit() only gates its cleanup on the driver\npointer being non-NULL, so it operates on the already-freed driver:\n\n    module_init(xhci_hcd_init)\n      xhci_hcd_init()\n        xhci_dbc_init()                       [return value ignored]\n          dbc_tty_init()\n            tty_register_driver() fails\n              tty_driver_kref_put()           -> driver freed\n              (dbc_tty_driver left dangling)\n    ...\n    module_exit(xhci_hcd_fini)\n      xhci_hcd_fini()\n        xhci_dbc_exit()\n          dbc_tty_exit()\n            if (dbc_tty_driver)               -> true (dangling)\n              tty_unregister_driver()         -> use-after-free", "datePublished": "2026-09-09T16:19:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01b7bc0938061f2fd46e0094f6483d8c6c02f7d3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43635ff6401ca0e0ed21875379eeded921321525", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eaca2814f32b9872a332326324b9e83e01f156d2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/943f976c93e70563b132f5585ff68b08c89641a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d0faf3cc44c4d86fc6faf5cea972c0fbe00b922", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/33ed35ca629477f57e0dd1d77d6df96cf5a9eb55", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e469b94fbba8eb03666da41dd1082b793c50c1a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a916fa66a43e10f63198b6ce978badffc678821a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80923", "GHSA-m8fv-jwwg-rhrm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01867db1-39c7-3a17-9cda-d3a75a6964f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0ef3cc4a-5b80-36b9-8e18-2124eac4a199", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.220"}, {"id": "1208df9b-4b8c-3073-a2b2-ae58a9c31d9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4521f16139409cdf9462c7325d43454462cff6c3 <0e469b94fbba8eb03666da41dd1082b793c50c1a"}, {"id": "1610c58e-d5fb-3297-9085-a23a248a3309", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4521f16139409cdf9462c7325d43454462cff6c3 <0d0faf3cc44c4d86fc6faf5cea972c0fbe00b922"}, {"id": "1b848b19-6667-372a-9aa6-b51b5783d964", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4521f16139409cdf9462c7325d43454462cff6c3 <eaca2814f32b9872a332326324b9e83e01f156d2"}, {"id": "1f5504cb-1671-367c-b119-4bcef701383d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4521f16139409cdf9462c7325d43454462cff6c3 <43635ff6401ca0e0ed21875379eeded921321525"}, {"id": "4fd089f0-2786-3c25-8e58-d7511c412a6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4521f16139409cdf9462c7325d43454462cff6c3 <01b7bc0938061f2fd46e0094f6483d8c6c02f7d3"}, {"id": "61f415e9-9b1d-3979-a4a8-e91dc6f4fee0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.13"}, {"id": "6d6bc114-c853-339f-ab6a-27f267b3d7cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "7b15b9a1-3452-3911-bb0c-04a4983fa367", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.49"}, {"id": "ccc72b4d-db83-3bed-858e-351fcc94db6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4521f16139409cdf9462c7325d43454462cff6c3 <a916fa66a43e10f63198b6ce978badffc678821a"}, {"id": "d2c5239b-9ebf-31f8-b012-714744eb4322", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name":